Janis Papanagnou <Janis_Papanagnou@hotmail.com> writes:
> [ un-id'ed potion cleared by unihorn ]
> ...it is one of blindness, confusion, hallucination.

The effects of any one of which, should you drink the potion, can be
easily and quickly fixed by [a]pplying a non-cursed unicorn horn.

Thus, depending on which other bad potions you already know, it _may_
be a smart idea to quaff unidentified, known-non-cursed potions. You
can get a more certain ID.

OTOH, drinking a potion whose effect you don't need is, aside from
identification, a waste. Dipping at least gets you water, which is
always useful. (Blindness and confusion can both be handy, though a
towel and casting a stale spell are, respectively, better ways to get
these things than a heavy, delicate, one-use potion which could be
used for water or alchemy. I know of no practical use for
hallucination.)

